<li about="#cite_note-Schuur2022-10" id="cite_note-Schuur2022-10" data-mw-footnote-number="10"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwBJI"><a href="./تغير_المناخ_في_آسيا#cite_ref-Schuur2022_10-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwBJM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwBJQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Schuur2022-10" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r70318604" about="#mwt95" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}' id="mwBJU"/><cite id="CITEREFSchuurAbbottCommaneErnakovich2022" class="citation journal cs1">Schuur، Edward A.G.؛ Abbott، Benjamin W.؛ Commane، Roisin؛ Ernakovich، Jessica؛ Euskirchen، Eugenie؛ Hugelius، Gustaf؛ Grosse، Guido؛ Jones، Miriam؛ Koven، Charlie؛ Leshyk، Victor؛ Lawrence، David؛ Loranty، Michael M.؛ Mauritz، Marguerite؛ Olefeldt، David؛ Natali، Susan؛ Rodenhizer، Heidi؛ Salmon، Verity؛ Schädel، Christina؛ Strauss، Jens؛ Treat، Claire؛ Turetsky، Merritt (2022). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1146%2Fannurev-environ-012220-011847" class="external text" id="mwBJY">"Permafrost and Climate Change: Carbon Cycle Feedbacks From the Warming Arctic"</a>. <i id="mwBJc">Annual Review of Environment and Resources</i>. ج.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBJg"> </span>47: <span class="nowrap" id="mwBJk">343–</span>371. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./بيب_كود" title="بيب كود" id="mwBJo">Bibcode</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2022ARER...47..343S" class="external text" id="mwBJs">2022ARER...47..343S</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./معرف_الغرض_الرقمي" title="معرف الغرض الرقمي" id="mwBJw">DOI</a>:<span class="id-lock-free" title="يمكن الوصول إليها بحرية" id="mwBJ0"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1146%2Fannurev-environ-012220-011847" class="external text" id="mwBJ4">10.1146/annurev-environ-012220-011847</a></span>. <q id="mwBJ8">Medium-range estimates of Arctic carbon emissions could result from moderate climate emission mitigation policies that keep global warming below 3<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBKA"> </span>°C (e.g., RCP4.5). This global warming level most closely matches country emissions reduction pledges made for the Paris Climate Agreement...</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Annual+Review+of+Environment+and+Resources&amp;rft.atitle=Permafrost+and+Climate+Change%3A+Carbon+Cycle+Feedbacks+From+the+Warming+Arctic&amp;rft.volume=47&amp;rft.pages=%3Cspan+class%3D%22nowrap%22%3E343-%3C%2Fspan%3E371&amp;rft.date=2022&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1146%2Fannurev-environ-012220-011847&amp;rft_id=info%3Abibcode%2F2022ARER...47..343S&amp;rft.aulast=Schuur&amp;rft.aufirst=Edward+A.G.&amp;rft.au=Abbott%2C+Benjamin+W.&amp;rft.au=Commane%2C+Roisin&amp;rft.au=Ernakovich%2C+Jessica&amp;rft.au=Euskirchen%2C+Eugenie&amp;rft.au=Hugelius%2C+Gustaf&amp;rft.au=Grosse%2C+Guido&amp;rft.au=Jones%2C+Miriam&amp;rft.au=Koven%2C+Charlie&amp;rft.au=Leshyk%2C+Victor&amp;rft.au=Lawrence%2C+David&amp;rft.au=Loranty%2C+Michael+M.&amp;rft.au=Mauritz%2C+Marguerite&amp;rft.au=Olefeldt%2C+David&amp;rft.au=Natali%2C+Susan&amp;rft.au=Rodenhizer%2C+Heidi&amp;rft.au=Salmon%2C+Verity&amp;rft.au=Sch%C3%A4del%2C+Christina&amp;rft.au=Strauss%2C+Jens&amp;rft.au=Treat%2C+Claire&amp;rft.au=Turetsky%2C+Merritt&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdoi.org%2F10.1146%252Fannurev-environ-012220-011847&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Far.wikipedia.org%3A%D8%AA%D8%BA%D9%8A%D8%B1+%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D9%86%D8%A7%D8%AE+%D9%81%D9%8A+%D8%A2%D8%B3%D9%8A%D8%A7" class="Z3988" id="mwBKE"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Phiddian2022-11" id="cite_note-Phiddian2022-11" data-mw-footnote-number="11"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwBKI"><a href="./تغير_المناخ_في_آسيا#cite_ref-Phiddian2022_11-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwBKM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwBKQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Phiddian2022-11" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r70318604" about="#mwt100" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}' id="mwBKU"/><cite id="CITEREFPhiddian2022" class="citation web cs1">Phiddian، Ellen (5 أبريل 2022). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://cosmosmagazine.com/earth/climate/explainer-ipcc-scenarios/" class="external text" id="mwBKY">"Explainer: IPCC Scenarios"</a>. <i id="mwBKc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Cosmos_(magazine)?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="Cosmos (magazine)" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["Cosmos (magazine)"]}}' id="mwBKg">Cosmos</a></i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20230920224129/https://cosmosmagazine.com/earth/climate/explainer-ipcc-scenarios/" class="external text" id="mwBKk">مؤرشف</a> من الأصل في 2023-09-20<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwBKo">. اطلع عليه بتاريخ <span class="nowrap" id="mwBKs">2023-09-30</span></span>. <q id="mwBKw"><span class="cs1-kern-left" id="mwBK0"></span>"The IPCC doesn't make projections about which of these scenarios is more likely, but other researchers and modellers can. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./The_Australian_Academy_of_Science?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="The Australian Academy of Science" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["The Australian Academy of Science"]}}' id="mwBK4">The Australian Academy of Science</a>, for instance, released a report last year stating that our current emissions trajectory had us headed for a 3<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBK8"> </span>°C warmer world, roughly in line with the middle scenario. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Climate_Action_Tracker?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="Climate Action Tracker" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["Climate Action Tracker"]}}' id="mwBLA">Climate Action Tracker</a> predicts 2.5 to 2.9<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBLE"> </span>°C of warming based on current policies and action, with pledges and government agreements taking this to 2.1<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwBLI"> </span>°C.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Cosmos&amp;rft.atitle=Explainer%3A+IPCC+Scenarios&amp;rft.date=2022-04-05&amp;rft.aulast=Phiddian&amp;rft.aufirst=Ellen&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fcosmosmagazine.com%2Fearth%2Fclimate%2Fexplainer-ipcc-scenarios%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Far.wikipedia.org%3A%D8%AA%D8%BA%D9%8A%D8%B1+%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D9%86%D8%A7%D8%AE+%D9%81%D9%8A+%D8%A2%D8%B3%D9%8A%D8%A7" class="Z3988" id="mwBLM"></span></span></li>
